]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Mb53RdgeBVPWtNQc7cdiKw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of 18%. The release candidate v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback, the service is healthy with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n1. **Problem:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, was also unhealthy.\n2. **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release marked healthy, and it's now running in all three regions. A follow-up check shows the service healthy with a 0.2% error rate. No approval was needed, since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure and the rollback, and notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 problem needs to be found before it's redeployed. The first attempt to create it timed out. The incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which prevents a duplicate incident and a second page.", "type": "text"}]}]}